  "id": "COMPOUND:40572 - PROTEIN:5837",
  "verbalization": "Caragasinin B is implicated in the biological pathway leading to SN12K1 through multiple indirect routes. The evidence suggests that Caragasinin B acts as a target for two distinct compounds, M059J and Plakortide N, which in turn target SN12K1. This indicates that Caragasinin B may function as a bridge in the signaling cascade, connecting different molecular entities that ultimately influence SN12K1. The shared target of Lup-20(29)-en-3-ol, (3beta)- across these pathways further supports a potential role for Caragasinin B in modulating the activity of this compound. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism where Caragasinin B influences the downstream effects of Lup-20(29)-en-3-ol, potentially through a common intermediate. The evidence does not definitively establish a direct interaction between Caragasinin B and SN12K1, but rather suggests a complex network of targets and interactions that may underlie the observed effects.",
